# Icons that browsers and link previews ask for at fixed addresses. Cloudflare answers these from the
# assets without running the Worker, where a missing file would render the 404 page.
/apple-touch-icon.png /icons/apple-touch-icon.png 301
/apple-touch-icon-precomposed.png /icons/apple-touch-icon.png 301
# The home address opens the app, since an installation has no page there: everything about BubbleBoard
# itself is on Commit's site (docs/adr/0002-the-site-is-commits-alone.md). Here rather than in a hook, so
# Cloudflare answers it without running the Worker, which spends none of the daily requests that the
# installations in one Cloudflare account share. A 302, because browsers keep a 301 for good. A rule
# matches its path exactly, so `/en/` has one of its own. A card's fragment comes along, though printed
# cards link to the app itself (src/lib/card.ts).
/ /app 302
/en /en/app 302
/en/ /en/app 302
